<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inverness</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inverness is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-highlands">Highlands of Scotland</a>, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-ness">River Ness</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moray-firth">Moray Firth</a>. The nearby hill fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/craig-phadrig">Craig Phadrig</a> and the area around the Ness are associated with the Pictish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bridei-son-of-maelchon">Bridei son of Maelchon</a>, whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a> visited in the 560s. Inverness became a royal burgh in the twelfth century and is now the administrative centre of the Highland council area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inverness.jpg" alt="Inverness" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diliff · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverness_Castle,_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
